Complete the canonical-data boundary for live subagent workspace and inspector state, branch-summary operation state, plugin UI presentation and permission/question prompt state. Inspect app/tui/subagent_workspace.*, TuiBranchSummarySnapshot, coordinator/inspector callbacks in runtime.h, runtime_plugin_ui.*, runtime_prompts_internal.* and the corresponding app adapters. Backend-internal coordinator snapshots may remain internal, but neither those snapshots nor inspector frames containing backend contracts may be passed directly into the TUI. Publish sanitized neutral state into canonical UnlockedData domains and let TuiFrontEnd-owned projections form local views.

Preserve owner-bound opaque identifiers, generation-checked operations, path-free subagent projections, eviction handling, cancellation/promote authority, plugin invocation lifetime and branch-summary confirmation rules. Interactive decisions remain explicit correlated actions routed to backend policy; a frontend snapshot or dirty flag must never resolve a permission, consume a question or act as a capability. Multiple pending prompts and plugin requests require ordered, lossless delivery with completion/cancellation and shutdown semantics, not last-value-wins replacement. Terminal drawing and editor manipulation remain local frontend responsibilities.

Remove transported Snapshot/Frame/view state from these callback contracts, retaining only narrowly justified neutral action or ordered-interaction control contracts documented in the inventory. Verify no stale inspector data survives owner/session changes, no canceled invocation accepts a late response, and no permission authority leaks into canonical presentation data. Run subagent workspace, branch summary, plugin UI, question and permission regression tests plus relevant real terminal interaction scenarios. This goal is not satisfied by declaring these old snapshot paths exempt because they are narrower than TuiRuntimeStateSnapshot.
